/*  A function puts its argument into a table it makes, then stores what it makes into that element.
    Obligation broken: O2, a store needs to know exactly where its target lives. See docs/SOUNDNESS.md.  */

Bind void to fill, given (the series of series of number rows):
    Define table as a series of series of series of number.
    Insert rows into table.
    Insert (a series of number with (1, 2, 3)) into item 1 of table.
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast fill on (keeper).
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper.
